SMITER software from UKAEA
--------------------------
SMITER = SMARDDA for ITER ; for a description of the SMARDDA algorithm for fieldlines
see http://dx.doi.org/10.1109/TPS.2014.2320904 (also http://arxiv.org/abs/1403.7142 )
SMITER has been tested on CentOS 7.0, Ubuntu 14.04 and Red Hat 4.4 (Scientific Linux),
also MacOS, 64-bit.
bash shell release 3.2 or later (i.e. from 2005 or later) is needed.
ParaView 4.4 for 64-bit linux may be downloaded separately from www.paraview.org to directory ??
(and needs to be set up so that it can be invoked by typing paraview at the command prompt).

If you are using pre-installed software, then the install script can be replaced by
export SMITER_DIR=~smiter
export SMITER_DOC=$SMITER_DIR/doc/srcdoc/html
export PATH=$SMITER_DIR/exec:$PATH
export PATH=??/ParaView-4.4.0-Qt4-Linux-64bit/bin/:$PATH

You may find it a good idea to ensure
that SMITER_DIR is always set by modifying your .bashrc file, by adding the above lines

The script ismiter guides the user interactively through the setting up of a basic test
case, starting with the sub-class of MSC Nastran-TM .dat files output by CATIA-TM.
ismiter has a significant inbuilt help capability
For efficient ismiter interaction with ParaView, the following settings are needed:
Settings->General, Click on gearwheel, untick Show Splash Screen, tick AutoApply (near top)
(Also useful is parallel projection:
[vtk file loaded] -> Properties tab, Click gearwheel, tick Camera Parallel projection (near bottom)

See SMITER user manual webpages for further details of (i)smiter use.
file://$SMITER_DOC/index.html

Note that the CADfix-TM interface between CATIA-TM and SMARDDA/SMITER is not 
well documented, and effective use of the commercially licensed
CADfix software requires a significant amount of training.
Paraview can also be used to convert triangulated surface geometries from a number
of different packages into the legacy (ASCII) vtk format.

The directory ~warter/smiteraux contains the smiter test deck and should be
copied into the user's home space. The file tests.bash runs the text-deck.

The script tes.sgo in $SMITER_DIR/Extras show how SMITER works in detail, given the
necessary geometry in legacy vtk format. Detailed descriptions of the namelists in the .ctl
files (which control execution) may be found by pointing a browser at
file://$SMITER_DOC/classes.html

